; Consumer spec for the LOCAL-MINT-UNDER-A-DEP-INDEXED-NAME backstop: both arms of
; `try_defer_wrapper` that return before any index is consulted, each minting a class whose name the
; dependency's index also lists. The class emitted is the same duplicate-`#[wasm_bindgen]`-symbol
; configuration the rule-declared table flavor warns about, reached by paths that used to warn
; nothing — which is why the honesty check lives at the mint seam (`record_collection_wrapper`)
; rather than on any one `return false`.
;
;   * IDENT≠STRUCTURAL arm (`arr_idx_foo_list`): its element is the RULE `idx_foo_list`, so the
;     structurally-derived name is `IdxFooListList` while the emitted class is the rule's own
;     `ArrIdxFooList` — a name the dep's index lists. The screen at the top of `try_defer_wrapper`
;     declines on the structural name and never looks at the emitted one.
;   * R3c CONSTITUENT arm (`idx_hash_list`): ident and structural name coincide (`IdxHashList`,
;     which the dep's index also lists), but the element `idx_hash` is CONSUMER-owned, so the
;     all-one-dep screen returns local-and-silent. That is right about the DEFERRAL — the consumer
;     genuinely owns the element — and says nothing about the NAME.
;
; `idx_foo_list` itself is the already-pinned unification cell (it defers, and warns that it does),
; kept here deliberately: it is what makes `arr_idx_foo_list`'s element a named consumer rule, and it
; proves the two warnings coexist without either suppressing the other through the shared
; once-per-ident set.
idx_foo_list = [* idx_foo]

arr_idx_foo_list = [* idx_foo_list]

; Consumer-owned element whose structural list name the dep's index lists.
idx_hash = [a: uint]

idx_hash_list = [* idx_hash]

holder = [a: arr_idx_foo_list, b: idx_hash_list]
